        "target": "Given that Mrs. Snyder used to spend 40% of her monthly income on rent and utilities, and after a $600 salary increase, this amount now constitutes 25% of her new income, I started by defining the unknown: her previous monthly income, which I denoted as \\( x \\).\n\nFrom the problem, I derived two key pieces of information:\n1. \\( 0.4x \\) was her previous expenditure on rent and utilities.\n2. After the $600 increase, her new income is \\( x + 600 \\), and 25% of this new income is \\( 0.25(x + 600) \\).\n\nSince the amount spent on rent and utilities is the same in both scenarios, I set up the equation:\n\\[ 0.4x = 0.25(x + 600) \\]\n\nExpanding and simplifying the equation:\n\\[ 0.4x = 0.25x + 150 \\]\n\\[ 0.4x - 0.25x = 150 \\]\n\\[ 0.15x = 150 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{150}{0.15} \\]\n\\[ x = 1000 \\]\n\nTo verify the solution, I checked if 40% of $1000 is indeed equal to 25% of the new income after a $600 increase:\n\\[ 0.4 \\times 1000 = 400 \\]\n\\[ 0.25 \\times (1000 + 600) = 0.25 \\times 1600 = 400 \\]\n\nBoth sides of the equation are equal, confirming that my solution is correct.\n\nFINAL: 1000",
